1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:07,470
This video shows you how to run a route on only some of your workers, with a worker group.

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:11,342
Two workers in the standalone group run every route.

3
00:00:11,342 --> 00:00:17,670
A new site, edge, gets a worker of its own, and a topic of its own, smeltr-edge-in.

4
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:22,535
Open Admin, Worker groups, and add a group called edge.

5
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:32,540
A group is configuration, so it goes on a branch, edge-group.

6
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:35,430
It stays Pending until you deploy it.

7
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:40,094
Open Build, and switch from Shared configuration to edge.

8
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:50,738
The routes from shared configuration come first.

9
00:00:50,738 --> 00:00:53,234
Every worker group runs them.

10
00:00:53,920 --> 00:01:00,843
Add a route for edge, from a new Kafka source, edge-in, that reads smeltr-edge-in.

11
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:18,033
A group's route can use shared pipelines and destinations.

12
00:01:18,033 --> 00:01:22,763
Send it through tutorial-in-parse to tutorial-out, and save.

13
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:27,092
Open it for review, and deploy it.

14
00:01:27,092 --> 00:01:29,275
The group goes live.

15
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:38,273
Now enroll a worker into edge.

16
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:44,364
Under Admin, Workers, Enrollment codes, add a code for the edge group.

17
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:48,910
The settings it gives you name the group.

18
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:53,121
Start the edge worker with them, as you did in Getting started.

19
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:00,523
Status now lists three workers across two worker groups.

20
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:05,149
On Map, each group has a panel of its own.

21
00:02:05,149 --> 00:02:08,870
Under edge, edge-in flows to tutorial-out.

22
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:12,076
tutorial-in shows 0 rows a second under edge.

23
00:02:12,076 --> 00:02:13,198
That's expected.

24
00:02:13,198 --> 00:02:19,019
Shared configuration runs in every group, so the edge worker reads tutorial-in too.

25
00:02:19,019 --> 00:02:21,754
It shares tutorial-in's consumer group,

26
00:02:21,754 --> 00:02:27,110
and Kafka gave both of tutorial-in's partitions to the standalone workers.

27
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:29,110
Check on learning.

28
00:02:29,310 --> 00:02:34,538
Why does tutorial-in show 0 rows a second under edge?

29
00:02:38,938 --> 00:02:42,241
Shared configuration runs in every worker group.

30
00:02:42,241 --> 00:02:45,819
The edge worker shares tutorial-in's consumer group,

31
00:02:45,819 --> 00:02:49,997
and Kafka gave both of its partitions to standalone.

32
00:02:50,897 --> 00:02:54,984
Next, move a pipeline to another leader.
